SCOPE & CONTACT
This policy explains how Puckbound Hockey handles information for the game and its cloud team service. For privacy questions or requests, contact Puckboundhockey@gmail.com. Do not send your private Team ID or sign-in credentials by email.
GAMEPLAY & ACCOUNT DATA
We store your team name, player names and customizations, roster, lineup, equipment, coins, Bucks, results, match history and reward progress in the cloud and on your device. The service also stores internal account identifiers, credential hashes, save revisions and account/session timestamps. Sign-in uses a private Team ID, not an email address or password. Avoid putting personal information in team or player names.
DEVICE STORAGE
The game stores sign-in credentials, gameplay caches, sync checkpoints and local backups on your device. Native sign-in credentials use secure device storage; browser credentials use browser storage. Temporary team-creation data, including a creation key and save, is kept locally until creation succeeds. Music and SFX settings remain device-local. Name safety is always enabled for team, player and goalie names on the device and cloud service. Inappropriate submitted names are rejected; inappropriate names in older or imported saves are replaced with safe names while retaining gameplay progress. Automated name checks cannot detect every expression or language.
WHY WE USE INFORMATION
We use this information to create and restore teams, save progress, synchronize devices, apply your preferences, provide support and protect the service. Network requests expose technical information such as IP addresses to service and hosting providers. The game service uses hashed IP-derived keys for short-lived request rate limiting. When you contact support, we receive your email address and the information you choose to send and use it to address your request.
SERVICE PROVIDERS & AUDIO
Hosting and infrastructure providers process game data and network information to operate the cloud service. Remote audio hosts receive requests when sounds or music download, which may be cached on your device. In embedded web previews, error messages, timestamps and optional stack traces may be sent to the preview host for troubleshooting. Provider processing may occur outside your country and is subject to applicable safeguards and the provider’s practices.
PURCHASES, ADS & PERMISSIONS
Bucks checkout is disabled in this version, so the game does not collect payment details or process live purchases. We will update this policy before enabling purchases. The current game does not use advertising tracking or request your contacts, precise location, camera or microphone for gameplay. We do not sell your personal information or use it for targeted advertising.
RETENTION & DELETION
Cloud gameplay is retained while your team exists. Logout revokes this device’s session and removes its sign-in credentials, but keeps the cloud team and a local gameplay backup. Options → DELETE TEAM removes the active team and related sessions from the live service, invalidates its Team ID and clears associated account/gameplay storage on this device. Music and SFX settings remain. Other devices may keep cached data until refreshed or cleared. Infrastructure backups, security records and support correspondence may be retained for operational or legal needs; deletion from the live service does not promise immediate erasure from every provider backup.
YOUR CHOICES & RIGHTS
You can view your team information in the game, change names and preferences, log out or delete your team in Options. Your local data can also be cleared through your device or browser settings. Depending on your location, you may have rights to access, correct, delete or restrict personal information, obtain a copy or complain to your local data-protection authority. Contact Puckboundhockey@gmail.com to request help; we may need to verify a request without asking you to email private credentials. A lost Team ID cannot be recovered.
CHILDREN & SECURITY
We do not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13, or below the applicable local age, without legally required permission. A parent or guardian who believes a child supplied personal information can contact Puckboundhockey@gmail.com. Keep the Team ID private and use secure devices. We use credential hashing and separate device sessions, but no storage or transmission system can be guaranteed completely secure.
